  "slug": "concentrate-contacts-62cb",
  "summary": "New work treats cold-start and cross-site generalization as auditable targets, pairing leakage-aware evaluation with shift-oriented models in drug and neuroimaging ML.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is making generalization and reliability explicit and checkable in biomedical ML. The DDI/DTI perspective frames cold-start evaluation as auditable claims, proposing an L0-L5 framework and a leakage checklist. Modeling papers target specific shifts: FedSPL shares embedding prototypes alongside model parameters to address scaffold heterogeneity in federated molecular property prediction, and MIRAGE-DTA uses modality masks, training-only retrieval and evidence arbitration for drug-target affinity prediction. The ANA preprint applies a related concern to neuroimaging, with an agentic LLM framework using fixed computational tools to search 71 pipelines for site-independent ASD classifiers from resting-state fMRI. What is new is the pairing of stricter evaluation protocols with methods designed for heterogeneity, conflicting evidence and cross-site transfer, though the items address these in different domains.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
